redstonepanel (1.9.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Java servers can be Paper or Fabric as well as vanilla, on a chosen
    Minecraft release (the newest by default).
  * Each Java server runs the Java its Minecraft version needs, from
    /usr/lib/jvm; deploy and update name the openjdk package to install
    when no installed Java is new enough.
  * Update can move a Java server to a newer Minecraft release, never an
    older one, and downloads before stopping the server.
  * Vanilla and Paper downloads are checked against their checksums.

