redstonepanel (1.8.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Notifications: a Discord or JSON webhook for crashed, started and
    stopped servers, scheduled restarts and finished or failed backups
    (Panel Settings > Notifications). Server events come from a systemd
    drop-in for every minecraft-*.service, so crashes are reported while
    the panel is stopped. New command: redstonepanel notify-test.
  * Scheduled restarts with in-game warnings (Maintenance tab), as
    redstonepanel-restart@<server>.timer. New command: redstonepanel
    restart-server NAME.
  * The console colours lines by kind.
  * Fixed: a crashed Bedrock server was never restarted (screen exits 0
    when the game dies). It now starts again after 20 seconds.
  * Fixed: a stopped Java server (exit 143) showed as failed.
  * Fixed: dark mode's white workspace and unreadable New Server title.

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:33:34 +0000

redstonepanel (1.7.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Scheduled backups. Each server's Backups tab sets a schedule (hourly,
    every 6 or 12 hours, daily or weekly) run by a systemd timer,
    redstonepanel-backup@<server>.timer, so backups happen while the panel
    is stopped. Archives go to /var/backups/redstonepanel/<server>/ (root
    only); scheduled ones are pruned to the number kept.
  * Consistent copies of running servers: save-off/save-all flush/save-on
    over RCON for Java, save hold/save query/save resume for Bedrock.
  * Back up now, download, delete, and restore a backup over the current
    world (admins). The replaced world is kept as a "Before restore"
    backup.
  * New command: redstonepanel backup NAME.
  * Uninstalling a server removes its backup timer and keeps its backups;
    restoring the server brings the schedule back.

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:03:34 +0000

redstonepanel (1.6.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Restore removed servers. Servers uninstalled with "Keep World" are
    listed under New Server > Removed servers (and by `redstonepanel
    removed`); restoring writes a new systemd unit under the same name,
    keeps the old port unless another server took it, downloads the server
    binary only if it is missing, then enables and starts it. Also
    `redstonepanel restore NAME`.
  * "Uninstall (Keep World)" now keeps the server binary too, so a restore
    runs the same game version, and remembers the server's heap size.
  * Admins can permanently delete a removed server's files.
  * Uninstall refuses names that aren't the panel's own servers.
  * Parallel deploys and imports can no longer pick the same server name.

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:11:12 +0000

redstonepanel (1.5.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Clusters: make one panel the master and add other panels as nodes with
    single-use join codes. The master's Cluster page lists every node's game
    servers and can start, stop and restart them. A cluster CA issues each
    member's HTTPS certificate, limited to private addresses and local names.
    Node tokens only reach game-server listing and control, never users or
    settings. Encrypted backup and promote recover from a lost master.
  * New commands: cluster create/status/join-code/backup/promote, join,
    leave and cluster-https.
  * The header shows the panel's version, also returned by /api/auth/me.
  * The server action endpoint only accepts start, stop and restart for the
    panel's own minecraft* units.

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:57:09 +0000

redstonepanel (1.4.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Bedrock: show why players can't connect. The overview warns when the
    server rejected its transport (1.26.x accepts only NetherNet), when a
    NetherNet server started without accepting clients on its TCP port,
    and when server-udp-ports has a public address in front, which stops
    that listener on 1.26.63.1. The sidebar marks affected servers.
  * Detect Phantom proxies installed as services next to a Bedrock server,
    whatever their unit name, and flag the two ways they break it: holding
    UDP 19132 and forwarding to their own port ("Server offline").
  * NetherNet servers show their TCP signaling port and UDP gameplay ports.

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:03:49 +0000

redstonepanel (1.3.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix Java live chat failing with "not connected" when the RCON password
    contains symbols such as : = # ! or \, or spaces. Minecraft saves
    server.properties in Java's escaped format; the panel now reads and
    writes it the same way, so it uses the password the server uses.
    It also agrees with Minecraft on trailing spaces and continued lines,
    which could leave RCON switched off while the panel thought it was on;
    the panel now turns it back on and restarts the server.
  * Saving properties only rewrites the settings that changed.
  * Clearer chat errors: a rejected password or RCON not running now says
    to restart the server (needed after changing rcon.password).

 -- Quentin Russell <quentin.russell@cielocloud.org>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:04:35 +0000

redstonepanel (1.3.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Name each panel to tell several servers apart: the name shows in the
    sidebar, the browser tab title and on the sign-in page. It defaults to
    the host name; set it in Panel Settings or with
    "redstonepanel set-name NAME". "redstonepanel status" shows it.
  * Import server backups as .zip, .tar.gz/.tgz or .tar. A backup wrapped in
    a single folder (e.g. bedrock-server_backup_20261110/) is unpacked from
    inside it, so the server starts. Archives are unpacked safely (no paths
    or links outside the server folder) and the edition is detected from
    the files; non-backups are refused with a clear message.
  * Fix the generated systemd units: "RestartSec=20 5" was invalid.

